    "ground_truth_answer": "The Cash Conversion Cycle (CCC) is calculated as Days Inventory Outstanding (DIO) + Days Sales Outstanding (DSO) - Days Payable Outstanding (DPO).\nFor 2026:\nDIO = (Average Inventory / Cost of Goods Sold) * 365\nAverage Inventory = ($7,551 million + $8,170 million) / 2 = $7,860.5 million\nDIO = ($7,860.5 million / $43,362 million) * 365 = 66.2 days\nDSO = (Average Accounts Receivable / Net Sales) * 365\nAverage Accounts Receivable = ($6,185 million + $6,056 million) / 2 = $6,120.5 million\nDSO = ($6,120.5 million / $87,032 million) * 365 = 25.7 days\nDPO = (Average Accounts Payable / Cost of Goods Sold) * 365\nAverage Accounts Payable = ($15,227 million + $16,306 million) / 2 = $15,766.5 million\nDPO = ($15,766.5 million / $43,362 million) * 365 = 132.7 days\nCCC = DIO + DSO - DPO = -40.9 days (computed from unrounded components)\n\nFor 2025:\nDIO = (Average Inventory / Cost of Goods Sold) * 365\nAverage Inventory = ($7,016 million + $7,551 million) / 2 = $7,283.5 million\nDIO = ($7,283.5 million / $41,164 million) * 365 = 64.6 days\nDSO = (Average Accounts Receivable / Net Sales) * 365\nAverage Accounts Receivable = ($6,118 million + $6,185 million) / 2 = $6,151.5 million\nDSO = ($6,151.5 million / $84,284 million) * 365 = 26.6 days\nDPO = (Average Accounts Payable / Cost of Goods Sold) * 365\nAverage Accounts Payable = ($15,364 million + $15,227 million) / 2 = $15,295.5 million\nDPO = ($15,295.5 million / $41,164 million) * 365 = 135.6 days\nCCC = DIO + DSO - DPO = -44.4 days (computed from unrounded components)\n\nAnalysis: The Cash Conversion Cycle became less negative, from -44.4 days in 2025 to -40.9 days in 2026 (an increase of 3.5 days). P&G still collects cash from customers well before it pays its suppliers, but this advantage narrowed as inventory days rose and payable days fell.",
